rsoda
=====

rsoda is a Rust port of the LSODA ordinary differential equation solver
(automatic switching between Adams and BDF methods).

ODEPACK
-------
LSODA is part of ODEPACK, written by Alan C. Hindmarsh and Linda R. Petzold
at Lawrence Livermore National Laboratory (UC LLNL, contract W-7405-ENG-48
with the U.S. Department of Energy). The ODEPACK package has been declared
to be in the Public Domain. See the LICENSE file of the Reference
implementation for the full notice and disclaimer.

Fortran fork
------------
The port follows, and its Golden files are generated by, the thread-safe
Modern Fortran fork of ODEPACK by Nicholas Wogan:
https://github.com/Nicholaswogan/odepack

That fork carries the same public-domain declaration for the ODEPACK code.

No ODEPACK or fork source is copied into this repository; the Fortran driver
in fortran/ only calls it. Credit for the algorithm and its design belongs to
the ODEPACK authors.
